Which way the kernel runs along the edges the tests round (2026-09-18).

A temporary diagnostic line, printed after the stations are handed to the kernel in
geometry::variableFilletEdges(), and removed again before the qualification build:

    std::fprintf(stderr, "DIAGNOSTIC %s: spine %s\n", name.c_str(), forward ? "forward" : "reversed");

"forward": the kernel's spine starts at the end that comes first along the edge's canonical
direction; "reversed": it starts at the other end, and the stations are handed over as
1 - position, in reverse order. The Debug test executable ran the two test cases below;
the lines are counted by text:

  bettercad_tests.exe VariableFillet_RoundsIsolatedStraightEdges,VariableFilletFeature_FollowsItsBlockAndRadii

Both directions occur (the back edges of counter-clockwise profiles run -x), and the
uneven stations on the reversed edges pass the check of the kernel's law against
BetterCAD's, which a wrong mapping would fail.

 10 x DIAGNOSTIC edge reference 1 (line through (0, 0, 20) mm along (1, 0, 0)): spine forward
 10 x DIAGNOSTIC edge reference 2 (line through (0, 50, 20) mm along (1, 0, 0)): spine reversed
 11 x DIAGNOSTIC edge reference 1 (line through (0, 0, 40) mm along (1, 0, 0)): spine forward
